# ns_quickcheck.msg.en - message catalog for netscaler-quickcheck 17.43
# Format: KEY<TAB>text; placeholders %1..%9 in the order of the values in the script call
# --- TAG: Kennungen
TAG_OK	[OK]
TAG_INFO	[INFO]
TAG_WARN	[WARN]
TAG_YELLOW	[YELLOW]
TAG_RED	[RED]
TAG_ORANGE	[ORANGE]
TAG_TRUST	[TRUST]
TAG_ACTION	ACTION
TAG_RESULT	RESULT
# --- HDR: Kopf, Blockueberschriften, anon-Hinweise
HDR_CFG_FROM_SNAPSHOT_CONF	cli_user from ns_snapshot.conf
HDR_CFG_FROM_QUICKCHECK_CONF	cli_user from ns_quickcheck.conf
HDR_CVE_CONFLICT_COND_FRAG	%1 %2 (same fix, condition rules file %3, custom %4);
HDR_CVE_CONFLICT_FIX_FRAG	%1 %2 (rules file fix %3, custom fix %4);
HDR_ANON_COMMENT_REMOVED	# (comment removed)
HDR_CLI_REASON_NO_CLI	disabled by --no-cli
HDR_CLI_REASON_NO_USER	CLI_USER not set
HDR_CLI_REASON_NO_NSCLI	/netscaler/nscli missing
HDR_CLI_REASON_NO_SECRET	secret file missing
HDR_CLI_REASON_SECRET_PERMS	secret file not root:600
HDR_CLI_REASON_SECRET_EMPTY	secret file empty
HDR_RUN_LINE	ns_quickcheck %1  host=%2  mode=%3  window=%4h  rules=%5  cli=%6%7  %8
HDR_CUSTOM_LOADED	Operator custom file loaded: %1 active indicator line(s), %2 CVE line(s) (%3)
HDR_CUSTOM_NO_VERSION	no version
HDR_CVE_CONFLICT	Rules file and custom file rate %1 CVE differently. Both lines are checked, the stricter result counts: %2
HDR_RULES_OLDER	Rules file %1 is older than the minimum rules stand of this script (%2). Checks whose rules are missing are skipped with a note
HDR_TRUSTED_EXPIRED_FRAG	, %1 expired and skipped
HDR_TRUSTED_LIST	Trusted list: %1 entry/entries (ns_quickcheck.trusted_ips)%2. Trusted addresses appear as [TRUST], impact findings stay red
HDR_TRUSTED_BAD_LINES	Trusted list: line(s) %1 skipped (no IPv4 address; format: address ; until ; note)
HDR_TRUSTED_AND_BLOCKED	%1 is in trusted_ips and in the block list. The block list wins
HDR_BLOCKED_LIST	Block list: %1 entry/entries (ns_quickcheck.blocked_ips and appliance ACLs). Findings for blocked addresses before the block date become ORANGE (covered)%2
HDR_BLOCKED_NODATE_FRAG	; %1 without date: marked only. For ORANGE, enter the block date (YYYY-MM-DD) as the second field
HDR_BLOCKED_BAD_LINES	Block list: line(s) %1 skipped (no IPv4 address; format: address ; since ; note)
HDR_IOC_INACTIVE	Rules file format 2: %1 indicator line(s) inactive (source pending or marked for removal)
HDR_OFFLINE_SOURCE	Source: %1
HDR_CLI_OFF	CLI layer off: %1
HDR_CLI_REASON_NONE	no access path
HDR_WHITELIST_LOADED	Whitelist: %1 (%2 rules)
HDR_WL_WEBFILE_UNANCHORED	Whitelist: webfile rule(s) that end neither in / (directory) nor in $ (file) match more than intended: %1(README 15)
HDR_WL_DIR_RULES	Whitelist: %1 directory rule(s) without hash. They allow everything below, new files included (never code). Recommended: one pin per file, --pin-all <folder> (WORKFLOW, Whitelist)
HDR_WL_CODE_NO_PIN	Whitelist: file rule(s) on code without a hash pin have no effect. Code needs @sha256=<hash> (--pin <path> creates the lines): %1
HDR_WHITELIST_MISSING	Whitelist: not present (%1). All findings unfiltered
HDR_BLOCK1	1 Build
HDR_BLOCK2	2 Exposure
HDR_BLOCK3	3 Mitigation
HDR_BLOCK4	4 Attack traces (last %1h)
HDR_BLOCK5	5 Compromise quick check
HDR_BLOCK6	6 Verdict
HDR_ANON_REPORT_NOTE	# anonymized by mapping table (%1 entries%2). Attacker values, hashes, paths and rules stands unchanged. Spot-check before sharing.
HDR_ANON_SKIPPED_FRAG	; skipped as too short or a report word: %1
# --- BUILD: Block 1 Build
BUILD_FROM_NSCONF	Build taken from the ns.conf header (kern.bootfile not available)
BUILD_FALLBACK_TEXT_RCE	pre-auth RCE, actively exploited
BUILD_FALLBACK_TEXT_SAML	SAML DoS, CISA KEV
BUILD_UNKNOWN_YEL	Build not determinable - check 'show ns version'
BUILD_EOL_RED	Release %1 is end of life, no fix available (running: %2)
BUILD_TRAIN_UNKNOWN_YEL	Train %1 not in the rules file (%2) - check manually against the bulletin (running: %3)
BUILD_CVE_PENDING_FRAG	(fix build not yet published, rules stand %1. Until then: mitigation, blocks 2 and 3)
BUILD_CVE_FIX_INVALID_FRAG	%1 %2: fix build '%3' invalid
BUILD_CVE_COND_FRAG	 (condition: %1 configured)
BUILD_VULN_NOFIX_RED	Build %1 is VULNERABLE to %2 (%3), no fix build published: %4
BUILD_VULN_RED	Build %1 is VULNERABLE to %2 (%3), fixed in %4: %5
BUILD_TARGET	Target build for this train: %1-%2
BUILD_ALL_FIXED_OK	Build %1 contains all %2 fix(es) for %3%4%5
BUILD_FIX_NA_FRAG	, %1 CVE(s) without configured condition
BUILD_FIX_RULES_FRAG	 from the rules file
BUILD_FIX_SPLIT_FRAG	 (%1 rules file, %2 custom)
BUILD_RULES_ROW_YEL	Rules file: %1
BUILD_VULN_JSON_PREFIX	Vulnerable:
BUILD_CONF_NOT_SAVED_YEL	ns.conf was saved on %1, running is %2 - 'save ns config' after the upgrade is missing
BUILD_WARN_YEL	Build %1: %2
BUILD_STAGED_NOT_BOOTED_YEL	%1 is installed (%2) but not booted - reboot pending?
BUILD_LAST_BOOT	Last boot: %1 (%2 days)
# --- EXPO: Block 2 Exposure
EXPO_SAML_CVE_OPEN	SAML configured (SP=%1 IdP=%2) - SAML-dependent CVE open, see block 1
EXPO_SAML	SAML configured (SP=%1 IdP=%2)
EXPO_NO_SAML_OK	No SAML SP/IdP - SAML-dependent CVEs not relevant
EXPO_DTLS	DTLS active on %1 gateway vServer(s) (precondition for CVE-2026-88772; mitigated on a fixed build)
EXPO_NO_DTLS_OK	No DTLS on gateway vServers
EXPO_ISN_STEP_MISSING_YEL	Configuration step missing: set ns tcpParam -%1 (%2, %3) - stays open after the upgrade
EXPO_ISN_ACTIVE_OK	Enhanced ISN Generation active
EXPO_PARTITIONS	%1 admin partition(s) - check TCP parameters and ISN there separately
EXPO_MGMT_ON_SNIP_YEL	Management access on SNIP enabled: %1 - NITRO/GUI reachable. CVE-2026-88771 is also staged through failed NITRO logins
EXPO_MGMT_NSIP_UNKNOWN	Management portal: NSIP not determinable from ns.conf, ACL mitigation (CTX697263) not checked
EXPO_MGMT_NO_ACL_VULN_YEL	Management portal (PHP, CTX697263) on a vulnerable build without ACL protection: %1- until the update, restrict port 80/443 of these addresses to admin networks by ACL (Citrix recommendation)
EXPO_MGMT_NO_ACL_FIXED	Management portal without DENY ACL on port 80/443: %1(build fixed against CTX697263; an ACL is still advisable if the portal is reachable from outside the admin networks)
EXPO_MGMT_ACL_OK	Management portal: DENY ACLs on port 80/443 present for %1 (Citrix mitigation CTX697263)
EXPO_MGMT_ACL_RULE_MISSING	Management portal ACLs not checked: rule MGMT_ACL_RE missing in the rules file (%1; needs %2 or newer)
# --- MITIG: Block 3 Mitigation
MITIG_NONE_VULN_YEL	No responder or traffic policy with log poisoning or SAML patterns - the unfixed build has no mitigation at all
MITIG_NONE	No mitigation policy found (not required on a fixed build without traces)
MITIG_POLICY_UNBOUND_YEL	%1 policy %2 exists but is not bound anywhere
MITIG_RESPONDER_OFF_YEL	%1 policy %2 bound (%3), but the responder feature is OFF - the policy has no effect
MITIG_NO_AAA_REQUEST_YEL	%1 policy %2 bound (%3), but without -type AAA_REQUEST - it sees no logon traffic
MITIG_RESPONDER_BOUND_OK	%1 policy %2 bound (%3 vServer, %4 x AAA_REQUEST%5)
MITIG_POLICY_BOUND_OK	%1 policy %2 bound (%3 vServer)
MITIG_HITS	  Hits %1: %2 (since the last counter reset)
MITIG_HITS_DELTA	  Hits %1: %2 (+%3 since %4)
MITIG_DENYLIST_OK	Global Deny List AAA_REQUEST present (Console signatures)
MITIG_DENYLIST_NONE	No Global Deny List AAA_REQUEST (not configured)
MITIG_DENYLIST_UNKNOWN	Global Deny List: no statement possible
# --- TRACE: Block 4 Angriffsspuren (ohne Gateway-AAA)
TRACE_IOC_SOURCE_FRAG	 - Source: %1 %2
TRACE_DETAIL_MORE	... and %1 more (DETAIL_MAX=%2)
TRACE_BLOCKED_TAG_FRAG	 (blocked since %1%2)
TRACE_BLOCKED_TAG_NODATE_FRAG	 (blocked, date unknown: marked only%1)
TRACE_NET24_ROW	%1 (%2 address(es), %3 request(s))
TRACE_COV_NO_NSLOG_FRAG	 ns.log family missing in the window;
TRACE_COV_NO_HTTPACCESS_FRAG	 httpaccess missing in the window (dropper, probing, sources);
TRACE_COV_UNREADABLE_FRAG	 %1 log file(s) not readable;
TRACE_NSPROF_DIVERTED	nsprofmon_mgmt.pl lines (CPU snapshots with process command lines) diverted up front: %1. They are only checked for suspicious processes, so the quickcheck does not find itself
TRACE_LOGS_READ	Logs read in the window: ns.log/nsvpn/messages/notice %1, httpaccess %2, httperror %3, auth.log %4, httpaccess.log (management) %5, cron %6 file(s)%7
TRACE_LOGS_UNREADABLE_FRAG	, %1 not readable
TRACE_NO_NSLOG_YEL	No ns.log/nsvpn.log/messages in the window (path %1) - logs rotated or not in the snapshot
TRACE_INJ_COVERED_ORG	%1 logon line(s) with injection patterns (CVE-2026-88771 / log poisoning), %2 to %3 - covered: download host(s) blocked, build fixed:
TRACE_INJ_COVERED_HOST_DET	%1: %2, the attempt of %3 is earlier
TRACE_INJ_COVERED_TODO_DET	To do: nothing. A new attempt with this host after the block date would be red again.
TRACE_INJ_RED	%1 logon line(s) with injection patterns (CVE-2026-88771 / log poisoning), %2 to %3:
TRACE_INJ_SRC_LINES_FRAG	%1  in %2 of %3 line(s)
TRACE_INJ_SRC_MATCH_FRAG	%1  matches %2 of %3 attempt time(s)%4
TRACE_INJ_SRC_OFFSET_FRAG	, logs offset by %1h
TRACE_INJ_ONE_WAVE_FRAG	 (one wave)
TRACE_INJ_WHEN_DET	When:          %1 to %2, %3 line(s) on %4 packet engine(s)%5
TRACE_LOG_DET	Log:           %1
TRACE_INJ_RESULT_VULN_DET	Result:        Build %1 is vulnerable. The daily ns_monuploadd_err.pl may have executed these lines or may still do so.
TRACE_INJ_RESULT_COVERED_DET	Result:        covered. Build fixed, download host(s) blocked before the attempt. A new attempt with this host after the block date would be red again.
TRACE_INJ_MITIG_ANSWERED_FRAG	, the mitigation policy responded
TRACE_INJ_RESULT_NO_EFFECT_DET	Result:        attempt without effect. Build %1 is fixed against CVE-2026-88771%2.
TRACE_INJ_SAML_CAUTION_DET	Caution:       SAML is configured and a SAML CVE is open. Such an attempt can then take effect another way. Work through block 1 first.
TRACE_BLOCKED_SINCE_FRAG	, blocked since %1
TRACE_NO	no
TRACE_YES	yes
TRACE_RULES_YES_FRAG	yes (%1)
TRACE_INJ_DLHOST_DET	Download host: %1   Block list: %2   Rules file: %3   Address list: payload_download_host
TRACE_INJ_DLHOST_NONE_DET	Download host: none visible in the payload
TRACE_SRC_WEAK_FRAG	, weak
TRACE_INJ_SRC_RESPONDER_DET	Source:        %1 (from the responder line, %2)%3%4%5
TRACE_SRC_SAME_AS_DLHOST_FRAG	, same as the download host (loads from itself)
TRACE_INJ_SRC_ACCESS_DET	Source:        %1, %2%3 (behind NAT only the NAT address)%4%5
TRACE_INJ_SRC_UNKNOWN_RESP_DET	Source:        unknown. The responder rejected the request before the web server, the access log does not have it, and the policy logs no client address (README 15, Howto Responder-Quelle)
TRACE_INJ_SRC_UNKNOWN_NOREQ_DET	Source:        unknown. No logon request in the access log at attempt time (log for that time rotated, or the clocks differ by more than 14h)
TRACE_INJ_SRC_UNKNOWN_NOLOG_DET	Source:        unknown. No access log in the window
TRACE_INJ_TODO_VULN1_DET	To do:         1. Do not patch, do not restart. Back up logs and /var/core externally (runbook).
TRACE_INJ_TODO_VULN2_DET	               2. Read block 5: payload files, webshells, accounts. On a hit: incident process.
TRACE_TODO_NOTHING_BLOCK_DET	To do:         nothing. The next run shows whether the block holds.
TRACE_INJ_TODO_FW_DET	To do:         %1. Firewall and DNS logs: any connection from NSIP/SNIP to %2 since %3? None = attempt without effect.
TRACE_INJ_TODO_FETCH_LOG_DET	               %1. Get httpaccess-vpn.log for %2 from the snapshot set and review the logon requests at that second (client address, user agent).
TRACE_INJ_TODO_RESP_AUDIT_DET	               %1. Extend the responder policy with an audit message action that logs CLIENT.IP.SRC (README 15, Howto Responder-Quelle). Review firewall logs for %2.
TRACE_INJ_TODO_BLOCK_HOST_DET	               %1. Block the download host in the firewall and add it to ns_quickcheck.blocked_ips (address ; date ; note). This finding then becomes ORANGE.
TRACE_INJ_NONE_OK	No injection patterns in logon lines of the last %1h
TRACE_CRASH_ESCALATION_FRAG	escalation:
TRACE_CRASH_DIR_EMPTY_FRAG	, empty
TRACE_CRASH_DIR_EVENT_FRAG	directory %1%2, %3 min after boot
TRACE_CRASH_PROC_UNKNOWN	(unknown)
TRACE_CRASH_CORE_NOLOG_FRAG	core without log line
TRACE_CRASH_TRIG_FRAG	%1 %2 from %3;
TRACE_CRASH_CORES_FRAG	, %1 core evidence item(s)
TRACE_CRASH_HEAD	%1 crash event(s) in the window (Pitboss, kernel, Apache error log, /var/core; counted once per process and PID)%2
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_SAML_VULN	nsaaad with SAML on an unfixed build: the SAML CVE is probably being exploited
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_NSAAAD_REPEAT	nsaaad on a SAML gateway %1 times in one day: exploitation pattern (CTX697174/CTX697191) until proven otherwise
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_HTTPD_VULN	httpd on a vulnerable build (CTX697263): the vulnerable process crashes, that is the attack
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_PPE_DTLS	packet engine with DTLS errors in the same window: possible CVE-2026-88772 attempt
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_SAME_DAY	%1 crashes of the same process in one day
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_THREE_DAYS	the same process crashed on three or more days (%1; ns_quickcheck_observed_crashes.tsv)
TRACE_CRASH_WHY_TRIGGER	crash right after an external request: %1
TRACE_CRASH_RED	%1 - %2
TRACE_CRASH_HTTPD_FRAG	; httpd: check the relation to CTX697263
TRACE_CRASH_NSAAAD_SAML_FRAG	; nsaaad on a SAML gateway is an exploitation indicator, red on the second event
TRACE_CRASH_YEL	%1 - every crash needs an assessment%2%3
TRACE_CRASH_TRIGGER_DET	Trigger:       %1(addresses as crash_trigger in the address list)
TRACE_CRASHFILE_HEAD	# ns_quickcheck: crashes per process and day, cumulated across runs. Never delete
TRACE_CRASH_EVENTS_DET	Events (newest first; time, process, PID, signal, restart counter):
TRACE_CRASH_EVENT_CORE_FRAG	  core: %1
TRACE_CRASH_EVENT_ROW	%1  %2  pid %3  signal %4  restarts %5%6
TRACE_CRASH_CORES_DET	Core evidence in the window (files or directories under /var/core; back up before reboot, send to Citrix Support):
TRACE_CRASH_WHAT_DET	What happened: a daemon crashed and Pitboss restarted it. Without SAML and on a fixed build, nsaaad is usually an operational issue. httpd in the CTX697263 window and nsppe with DTLS errors are attack patterns.
TRACE_CRASH_TODO_DET	To do: back up /var/core. If it repeats or the process matches an open CVE: Citrix Support, incident process.
TRACE_CRASH_NONE_OK	No crashes in the window (Pitboss, kernel, Apache error log, /var/core)
TRACE_CORE_BOOT	Core directory %1 empty, created %2 (%3 min after boot): boot aftermath of the upgrade or reboot, not a crash. Check the content: ls -la %4 (CORE_BOOT_LEVEL=yellow turns it into an event)
TRACE_KERNEL_PANIC_RED	%1 kernel panic/trap line(s) in the window - kernel crash, clarify the cause with Citrix Support:
TRACE_KERNEL_MEM_YEL	%1 line(s) of kernel memory pressure (swap exhausted, processes killed) - with httpd or nsaaad a companion of out-of-memory attacks (PHP2Shell), otherwise an operational issue:
TRACE_REBOOT_UNEXPLAINED_YEL	Restart on %1 without a reboot/shutdown command in the audit log of the window - panic, watchdog, power loss or intervention. Clarify the reason
TRACE_NSAAAD_UNKNOWN_FORMAT	%1 nsaaad line(s) in a format the anchored patterns do not know (build %2). Please send them in anonymized so the pattern can be extended
TRACE_NSAAAD_LEGACY_YEL	%1 nsaaad crash line(s) (old pattern; rules file %2 does not know PITBOSS_RE/KERNEL_EXIT_RE) - clarify the cause
TRACE_NSAAAD_LEGACY_NONE_OK	No nsaaad crashes in the window (old pattern)
TRACE_CRASH_RULES_MISSING	Process crashes not checked: rules PITBOSS_RE/KERNEL_EXIT_RE missing in the rules file (%1)
TRACE_NSPROF_SUSPECT_YEL	%1 CPU snapshot(s) with a suspicious process (SUSPECT_PROC_RE) - time series for block 5:
TRACE_NSPROF_NONE_OK	No suspicious processes in the CPU snapshots
TRACE_NO_ACCESSLOG	Dropper requests, probing sources and injection sources not checked: no httpaccess* file in the window (%1h)
TRACE_DROP_COVERED_ORG	Requests to dropper transport paths from blocked addresses - covered:
